or`, exit code as evidence), **332-334** the INTEGRATION subject by sha, **335-338** `cat-file -e` for a file the tree must hold |\n| 3 | Release proof bound to the merged candidate's commit, void once that subject moves | `SKILL.md:486-497` — **486-488** binds to the MERGED candidate's sha, **490-492** voids on a later merge / new tip / amend / re-export / re-tag with the count oracle re-derived, **495-496** ties to `RELEASING.md` step 4's head-SHA match |\n| 4 | Prospective audited files-only amendment keeps the seal; one changing run identity voids it | `SKILL.md:438-461` — **438-444** the declaration must be in the seal at issue; **446-449** the four invariants (acceptance text, task identity, run identity, safety requirements); **452-456** replay → **THE SEAL IS KEPT**; **457-461** replay with a changed run identity → **THE SEAL IS VOID**, any other change needs a SUCCESSOR SEAL |\n| 5 | Pre-existing seals stay under the existing void conditions; unchanged acceptance text alone is refused | `SKILL.md:464-471` — **464-467** never retroactive, never inferred, stays governed by the existing void conditions unmodified; **467-470** *\"acceptance text never changed, therefore the seal still holds\"* is **REFUSED** over a moved subject; **470-471** retrofitting is itself an amendment to a sealed subject |\n\nThe existing `VOID CONDITIONS` block and automatic-void rule (`SKILL.md:428-436`) are **retained verbatim** — qualified, not deleted. The full task diff is `107 insertions, 0 deletions` in the one in-scope file; the installed twin at `.claude/skills/tickmarkr-overseer/SKILL.md` is a symlink to it, so byte-identity holds automatically.\n\n## Verification — what I did and did not run\n\nI ran **no vitest suite**. That is deliberate: this skill's own pre-run law 2 (`SKILL.md:283-286`) forbids a `vitest` probe of any size while a run is live, and the harness states the gates run the full suite. Instead I verified statically: scope confirmed via `git diff --numstat`; t